# cpdf — real-world examples

## Select pages

```sh
# Pages 1-3 and 6 into a new file
cpdf in.pdf 1-3,6 -o out.pdf

# Even pages only (2, 4, 6...)
cpdf in.pdf even -o out.pdf
```

## Merge and split

```sh
# Merge two PDFs into one
cpdf -merge in.pdf in2.pdf -o out.pdf

# Merge, then stamp a copyright on every page (AND chains operations)
cpdf -merge in.pdf in2.pdf AND -add-text "Copyright 2014" -o out.pdf

# Split into ten-page chunks: Chunk001.pdf, Chunk002.pdf...
cpdf -split in.pdf -o Chunk%%%.pdf -chunk 10

# Split on bookmark boundaries, naming files after bookmark labels
cpdf -split-bookmarks 0 in.pdf -o @N.pdf

# Read command-line arguments from a control file
cpdf -control control.txt
```

## Transform pages

```sh
# Scale page dimensions and contents 2x in both directions
cpdf -scale-page "2 2" in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Scale pages to fit US Letter
cpdf -scale-to-fit usletterportrait in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Shift contents 26pt right, 18mm up
cpdf -shift "26pt 18mm" in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Rotate page contents 90 degrees
cpdf -rotate-contents 90 in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Crop pages to 600x400 pts
cpdf -crop "0 0 600pt 400pt" in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Two-up imposition
cpdf -twoup-stack in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Insert blank pages after pages 1, 3 and 4
cpdf -pad-after 1,3,4 in.pdf -o out.pdf
```

## Encrypt, decrypt, compress

```sh
# 128-bit encryption: owner password 'fred', user password 'joe'
cpdf -encrypt 128bit fred joe in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Decrypt with the owner password
cpdf -decrypt in.pdf owner=fred -o out.pdf

# Compress / decompress data streams
cpdf -compress in.pdf -o out.pdf
cpdf -decompress in.pdf -o out.pdf
```

## Bookmarks, text, watermarks

```sh
# List bookmarks
cpdf -list-bookmarks in.pdf

# Add bookmarks from a prepared file
cpdf -add-bookmarks bookmarks.txt in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Stamp watermark.pdf onto every page
cpdf -stamp-on watermark.pdf in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Page number and date, top-left, Courier
cpdf -topleft 10 -font Courier -add-text "Page %Page\nDate %d-%m-%Y" in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Blacken all text
cpdf -blacktext in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Force all lines to at least 2pt wide
cpdf -thinlines 2pt in.pdf -o out.pdf
```

## Presentation mode

```sh
# Build a presentation: Split transition, 10s per slide, title page manual
cpdf -presentation in.pdf 2-end -trans Split -duration 10 -o out.pdf
```

## Metadata and viewer settings

```sh
# Set document title
cpdf -set-title "The New Title" in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Open with toolbar hidden
cpdf -hide-toolbar true in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Set XMP metadata from a file
cpdf -set-metadata metadata.xml in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Open showing two columns, starting on the right
cpdf -set-page-layout TwoColumnRight in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Open in full-screen mode
cpdf -set-page-mode FullScreen in.pdf -o out.pdf
```

## Annotations and attachments

```sh
# List annotations
cpdf -list-annotations in.pdf

# Copy annotations from one PDF to another
cpdf -copy-annotations from.pdf in.pdf -o out.pdf

# Attach a file / remove all attachments
cpdf -attach-file sheet.xls in.pdf -o out.pdf
cpdf -remove-files in.pdf -o out.pdf
```

## Homelab: shrink a scanned manual before dropping it on the media server

```sh
cpdf -compress scanned-manual.pdf -o /srv/docs/manual-small.pdf
```
